  "body": "https://www.w3.org/Bugs/Public/buglist.cgi?bug_status=UNCONFIRMED&bug_status=NEW&bug_status=ASSIGNED&bug_status=REOPENED&component=HTML5%20spec&f1=status_whiteboard&list_id=61030&o1=notequals&product=HTML%20WG&query_format=advanced&v1=whatwg-resolved contains some bugs we should consider cloning into this issue tracker. However, it needs to be done carefully, since a lot of the bugs there are only applicable to the outdated spec, or are spurious, or already exist in either this tracker or in [the legacy WHATWG Bugzilla](https://www.w3.org/Bugs/Public/buglist.cgi?component=HTML&list_id=59905&product=WHATWG&resolution=---).\n\nWe can leave this issue open as a tracking issue so that we don't forget about that bug list. If there are particular issues over there that seem high priority and aren't already in one of our trackers, we can clone them into this tracker (or just fix them). If there are issues over there that are fixed over here, you can add \"whatwg-resolved\" to their whiteboard to remove them from the above search link.\n",
